BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-start-of-daylight-saving-time-20270314@todaycelebrates.com
DTSTAMP:20261014T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270314
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270315
SUMMARY:The Start of Daylight Saving Time
DESCRIPTION:Daylight Saving Time begins on the second Sunday in March\, whe
 n clocks across most of the United States jump from 2:00 a.m. standard tim
 e to 3:00 a.m. daylight time and the evenings gain an hour of light. The s
 chedule is set by federal law\, the Uniform Time Act of 1966 as amended\, 
 and it has started in March only since 2007. Hawaii and most of Arizona do
  not take part.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/the-start-of-daylig
 ht-saving-time/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/the-start-of-daylight-sav
 ing-time/
CATEGORIES:Community
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
